
What needs root (this installer never runs sudo):
  - no active ufw or firewalld was detected. With another firewall, open 4443-4542/udp yourself
  - sessions start at boot: lingering could not be read; it will be tried, but not undone on uninstall. If it fails, as root:  loginctl enable-linger alice
Checking the latest release...

Termenbox 0.1.56 will be installed for alice, with no root (sessions run as alice):
  - the server  /home/alice/.local/bin/termenbox-server
  - tmux        /home/alice/.local/bin/termenbox-tmux (a pinned static build, used before any tmux on PATH)
  - state       /home/alice/.config/termenbox
  - a user service termenbox.service, and a daily update check (signed releases only), in /home/alice/.config/systemd/user
  - updates     channel stable, installed automatically (change with --channel, or edit update.toml in the journal directory)
  - UDP port    the server picks a free one from 4443-4542 on its first start and keeps it
Every change is recorded in /home/alice/.local/state/termenbox; undo them with: termenbox-server --journal-dir /home/alice/.local/state/termenbox --revert --dry-run, then --revert

Lingering could not be switched on: the server starts at login only. As root:  loginctl enable-linger alice
